strong Democratic national environment", "A late-September Sacramento Bee report described the race as virtually tied, the main counter-signal", "Pan holds a large outside-spending edge while Kiley retains incumbency and a bigger warchest"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point firmly to Pan: the redrawn D+5 seat, a favorable midterm environment, and a unanimous expert consensus for a Democratic flip, with markets pricing roughly 95% for Democrats. A single report of a tied race and Kiley's incumbency justify trimming the expected margin somewhat, but not enough to upend the Likely D picture.", "watch": "If additional polling confirms the reported tie rather than treating it as an outlier, this would move toward a genuine tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Kevin Kiley (I) is running.", "Kevin Kiley is an independent standing in for the Republican side."]}, "overview": "Kevin Kiley, the incumbent who advanced to the general as an independent standing on the Republican side, faces Democrat Richard Pan in a Sacramento-area seat redrawn to lean Democratic by about five points. The national midterm environment also favors Democrats, and every major expert rating calls this a Democratic flip, most rating it Safe or Solid. Prediction markets price a Democratic win at roughly 95 percent.\n\nThere are counterweights. Kiley has the incumbency advantage and has raised nearly three times what Pan has directly, though Pan benefits from about $1.4 million in outside support. A late-September Sacramento Bee report described the candidates as virtually tied, the one signal cutting against the consensus. The forecast still favors Pan by a solid but not overwhelming margin, with meaningful uncertainty given the thin public polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9603, "margin": 11.77}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.95, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24"